IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P2-art-17.l4 -- ARTICLE 17 OF REGULATION (EU) 2016/679: RIGHT TO ERASURE ('RIGHT TO BE FORGOTTEN') (layer 1).
-- Written by P2 (Sonnet 5.5).  Lines 225-240 of eu-gdpr-2016-679-consolidated-20160504.txt (the two heading lines of
-- Article 17 at 225-226 are `inert` headings).
-- Target compiler: main (build 1.6.112).  Answers: MAYBE BOOLEAN; MAYBE `Duty outcome` for paragraph 2; a DEONTIC for
-- each regulative rule.
--
-- WHOSE.  Paragraph 1 states ONE relation twice: "the data subject shall have the right to obtain from the controller the
-- erasure ... and the controller shall have the obligation to erase": the data subject's claim and the controller's duty.
-- It is one function, `Art 17(1) ...`, and the regulative rule is its correlative.
-- THE POINTS.  The six grounds of paragraph 1 and the five exceptions of paragraph 3 are one function each (the pattern
-- of P1's Art 6(1) and Art 9(2)): a point answers JUST TRUE when it holds and JUST FALSE when it does not, by an
-- inference from the chapeau ("where one of the following grounds applies", "to the extent that"): marginal reading (a),
-- listed for a lawyer.  The combining functions take the points' answers as MAYBE BOOLEANs.
-- ARTICLE 11(2): see P2-art-15.l4.
-- READING A RESULT (NOTES).  NOTHING means the Regulation does not answer on these facts; never read it as no.
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Art 17 action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 17(1) erase the personal data without undue delay`
    `Art 17(2) take reasonable steps, including technical measures, to inform the controllers which are processing the personal data of the erasure request`

§ `Article 17(1): the six grounds`

-- src:228 | (a) the personal data are no longer necessary in relation to the purposes for which they were collected or otherwise processed;
@ref Art 17(1)(a) (src:228)
GIVEN `the personal data are no longer necessary in relation to the purposes for which they were collected or otherwise processed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(1)(a) point (a) applies: the personal data are no longer necessary in relation to the purposes for which they were collected or otherwise processed` MEANS
    IF `the personal data are no longer necessary in relation to the purposes for which they were collected or otherwise processed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); an inference clause by clause, marginal reading (a)): "where one of the following grounds applies: (a) the personal data are no longer necessary in relation to the purposes for which they were collected or otherwise processed"

-- src:229 | (b) the data subject withdraws consent on which the processing is based according to point (a) of Article 6(1), or point (a) of Article 9(2), and where there is no other legal ground for the processing;
@ref Art 17(1)(b) (src:229)
GIVEN `the data subject withdraws consent on which the processing is based according to point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is another legal ground for the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(1)(b) point (b) applies: the data subject withdraws consent and there is no other legal ground for the processing` MEANS
    IF `the data subject withdraws consent on which the processing is based according to point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` AND NOT (`there is another legal ground for the processing`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): "(b) the data subject withdraws consent on which the processing is based according to point (a) of Article 6(1), or point (a) of Article 9(2), and where there is no other legal ground for the processing"

-- src:230 | (c) the data subject objects to the processing pursuant to Article 21(1) and there are no overriding legitimate grounds for the processing, or the data subject objects to the processing pursuant to Article 21(2);
@ref Art 17(1)(c) (src:230)
GIVEN `the data subject objects to the processing pursuant to Article 21(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are overriding legitimate grounds for the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject objects to the processing pursuant to Article 21(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(1)(c) point (c) applies: the data subject objects to the processing and there are no overriding legitimate grounds for it, or the objection is under Article 21(2)` MEANS
    IF (`the data subject objects to the processing pursuant to Article 21(1)` AND NOT (`there are overriding legitimate grounds for the processing`))
       OR `the data subject objects to the processing pursuant to Article 21(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): "(c) the data subject objects to the processing pursuant to Article 21(1) and there are no overriding legitimate grounds for the processing, or the data subject objects to the processing pursuant to Article 21(2)"

-- src:231 | (d) the personal data have been unlawfully processed;
@ref Art 17(1)(d) (src:231)
GIVEN `the personal data have been unlawfully processed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(1)(d) point (d) applies: the personal data have been unlawfully processed` MEANS
    IF `the personal data have been unlawfully processed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): "where one of the following grounds applies: ... (d) the personal data have been unlawfully processed"

-- src:232 | (e) the personal data have to be erased for compliance with a legal obligation in Union or Member State law to which the controller is subject;
@ref Art 17(1)(e) (src:232)
GIVEN `the personal data have to be erased for compliance with a legal obligation in Union or Member State law to which the controller is subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(1)(e) point (e) applies: the personal data have to be erased for compliance with a legal obligation in Union or Member State law` MEANS
    IF `the personal data have to be erased for compliance with a legal obligation in Union or Member State law to which the controller is subject`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): "(e) the personal data have to be erased for compliance with a legal obligation in Union or Member State law to which the controller is subject"

-- src:233 | (f) the personal data have been collected in relation to the offer of information society services referred to in Article 8(1).
@ref Art 17(1)(f) (src:233)
GIVEN `the personal data have been collected in relation to the offer of information society services referred to in Article 8(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(1)(f) point (f) applies: the personal data have been collected in relation to the offer of information society services referred to in Article 8(1)` MEANS
    IF `the personal data have been collected in relation to the offer of information society services referred to in Article 8(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): "(f) the personal data have been collected in relation to the offer of information society services referred to in Article 8(1)"

§ `Article 17(3): the five exceptions`

-- src:236 | (a) for exercising the right of freedom of expression and information;
@ref Art 17(3)(a) (src:236)
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for exercising the right of freedom of expression and information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(3)(a) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for exercising the right of freedom of expression and information` MEANS
    IF `the processing is necessary for exercising the right of freedom of expression and information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "to the extent that", read as the exception's own limit: marginal reading (a), fork F17-1; the other reading is NOTHING): "Paragraphs 1 and 2 shall not apply to the extent that processing is necessary: (a) for exercising the right of freedom of expression and information"

-- src:237 | (b) for compliance with a legal obligation which requires processing by Union or Member State law to which the controller is subject or for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller;
@ref Art 17(3)(b) (src:237)
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation which requires processing by Union or Member State law to which the controller is subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(3)(b) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation or for a task in the public interest` MEANS
    IF `the processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation which requires processing by Union or Member State law to which the controller is subject` OR `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "to the extent that", marginal reading (a), fork F17-1): "Paragraphs 1 and 2 shall not apply to the extent that processing is necessary: ... (b) for compliance with a legal obligation which requires processing by Union or Member State law to which the controller is subject or for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller"

-- src:238 | (c) for reasons of public interest in the area of public health in accordance with points (h) and (i) of Article 9(2) as well as Article 9(3);
@ref Art 17(3)(c) (src:238)
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for reasons of public interest in the area of public health` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 9(2)(h) point (h) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 9(2)(i) point (i) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 9(3) personal data referred to in paragraph 1 may be processed for the purposes referred to in point (h) of paragraph 2` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(3)(c) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for reasons of public interest in the area of public health` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the processing is necessary for reasons of public interest in the area of public health`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "to the extent that", marginal reading (a), fork F17-1): "Paragraphs 1 and 2 shall not apply to the extent that processing is necessary: ... (c) for reasons of public interest in the area of public health"
        IF `Art 9(2)(h) point (h) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `Art 9(2)(i) point (i) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `Art 9(3) personal data referred to in paragraph 1 may be processed for the purposes referred to in point (h) of paragraph 2` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `Art 9(2)(h) point (h) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `Art 9(2)(i) point (i) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `Art 9(3) personal data referred to in paragraph 1 may be processed for the purposes referred to in point (h) of paragraph 2` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "in accordance with", read with the same inference: marginal reading (a), fork F17-2; the other reading needs only one of points (h) and (i)): "in accordance with points (h) and (i) of Article 9(2) as well as Article 9(3)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): points (h) and (i) of Article 9(2) and Article 9(3) are P1's answers, and one of them does not answer on these facts

-- src:239 | (d) for archiving purposes in the public interest, scientific or historical research purposes or statistical purposes in accordance with Article 89(1) in so far as the right referred to in paragraph 1 is likely to render impossible or seriously impair the achievement of the objectives of that processing; or
@ref Art 17(3)(d) (src:239)
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for archiving purposes in the public interest, scientific or historical research purposes or statistical purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right referred to in paragraph 1 is likely to render impossible or seriously impair the achievement of the objectives of that processing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(3)(d) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for archiving, research or statistical purposes` MEANS
    IF `the processing is necessary for archiving purposes in the public interest, scientific or historical research purposes or statistical purposes`
       AND `the processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)`
       AND `the right referred to in paragraph 1 is likely to render impossible or seriously impair the achievement of the objectives of that processing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "to the extent that" and "in so far as", marginal reading (a), fork F17-1): "(d) for archiving purposes in the public interest, scientific or historical research purposes or statistical purposes in accordance with Article 89(1) in so far as the right referred to in paragraph 1 is likely to render impossible or seriously impair the achievement of the objectives of that processing"

-- src:240 | (e) for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims.
@ref Art 17(3)(e) (src:240)
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(3)(e) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims` MEANS
    IF `the processing is necessary for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "to the extent that", marginal reading (a), fork F17-1): "(e) for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims"

-- src:235 | 3. Paragraphs 1 and 2 shall not apply to the extent that processing is necessary:
-- src:236 | (a) for exercising the right of freedom of expression and information;
-- src:237 | (b) for compliance with a legal obligation which requires processing by Union or Member State law to which the controller is subject or for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller;
-- src:238 | (c) for reasons of public interest in the area of public health in accordance with points (h) and (i) of Article 9(2) as well as Article 9(3);
-- src:239 | (d) for archiving purposes in the public interest, scientific or historical research purposes or statistical purposes in accordance with Article 89(1) in so far as the right referred to in paragraph 1 is likely to render impossible or seriously impair the achievement of the objectives of that processing; or
-- src:240 | (e) for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims.
@ref Art 17(3) the five exceptions together (src:235-240)
GIVEN `Art 17(3)(a) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for exercising the right of freedom of expression and information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 17(3)(b) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation or for a task in the public interest` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 17(3)(c) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for reasons of public interest in the area of public health` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 17(3)(d) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for archiving, research or statistical purposes` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 17(3)(e) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(3) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 17(3)(a) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for exercising the right of freedom of expression and information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `Art 17(3)(b) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation or for a task in the public interest` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `Art 17(3)(c) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for reasons of public interest in the area of public health` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `Art 17(3)(d) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for archiving, research or statistical purposes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `Art 17(3)(e) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `Art 17(3)(a) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for exercising the right of freedom of expression and information` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `Art 17(3)(b) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation or for a task in the public interest` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `Art 17(3)(c) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for reasons of public interest in the area of public health` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `Art 17(3)(d) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for archiving, research or statistical purposes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `Art 17(3)(e) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply to the extent that processing is necessary for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "to the extent that" in each of the five points, marginal reading (a), fork F17-1): "Paragraphs 1 and 2 shall not apply to the extent that processing is necessary"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): at least one point is not decided by the facts the caller gave (not sure), and none holds

§ `Article 17(1): the right to erasure and the obligation to erase`

-- src:227 | 1. The data subject shall have the right to obtain from the controller the erasure of personal data concerning him or her without undue delay and the controller shall have the obligation to erase personal data without undue delay where one of the following grounds applies:
@ref Art 17(1) chapeau (src:227)
GIVEN `the person is the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 17(1)(a) point (a) applies: the personal data are no longer necessary in relation to the purposes for which they were collected or otherwise processed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 17(1)(b) point (b) applies: the data subject withdraws consent and there is no other legal ground for the processing` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 17(1)(c) point (c) applies: the data subject objects to the processing and there are no overriding legitimate grounds for it, or the objection is under Article 21(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 17(1)(d) point (d) applies: the personal data have been unlawfully processed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 17(1)(e) point (e) applies: the personal data have to be erased for compliance with a legal obligation in Union or Member State law` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 17(1)(f) point (f) applies: the personal data have been collected in relation to the offer of information society services referred to in Article 8(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 17(3) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(1) the data subject has the right to obtain from the controller the erasure of personal data concerning him or her and the controller has the obligation to erase them` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is the data subject` AND `the body is the controller`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The data subject shall have the right to obtain from the controller ... and the controller shall have the obligation": a grant to the data subject against the controller (entitlement-named, fork F15-1)
        IF `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, Article 11(2)): "Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply except where the data subject"
        IF `Art 17(3) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "shall not apply"): "Paragraphs 1 and 2 shall not apply to the extent that processing is necessary"
        IF (`Art 17(1)(a) point (a) applies: the personal data are no longer necessary in relation to the purposes for which they were collected or otherwise processed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `Art 17(1)(b) point (b) applies: the data subject withdraws consent and there is no other legal ground for the processing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `Art 17(1)(c) point (c) applies: the data subject objects to the processing and there are no overriding legitimate grounds for it, or the objection is under Article 21(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `Art 17(1)(d) point (d) applies: the personal data have been unlawfully processed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `Art 17(1)(e) point (e) applies: the personal data have to be erased for compliance with a legal obligation in Union or Member State law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `Art 17(1)(f) point (f) applies: the personal data have been collected in relation to the offer of information society services referred to in Article 8(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
           AND `Art 17(3) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `Art 17(1)(a) point (a) applies: the personal data are no longer necessary in relation to the purposes for which they were collected or otherwise processed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `Art 17(1)(b) point (b) applies: the data subject withdraws consent and there is no other legal ground for the processing` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `Art 17(1)(c) point (c) applies: the data subject objects to the processing and there are no overriding legitimate grounds for it, or the objection is under Article 21(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `Art 17(1)(d) point (d) applies: the personal data have been unlawfully processed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `Art 17(1)(e) point (e) applies: the personal data have to be erased for compliance with a legal obligation in Union or Member State law` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `Art 17(1)(f) point (f) applies: the personal data have been collected in relation to the offer of information society services referred to in Article 8(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): "where one of the following grounds applies"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a ground holds but paragraph 3 is not decided by the facts the caller gave, or a ground is not decided and none holds

GIVEN `Art 17(1) the data subject has the right to obtain from the controller the erasure of personal data concerning him or her and the controller has the obligation to erase them` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 17 action`
`Art 17(1) the controller must erase the personal data without undue delay` MEANS
    IF `Art 17(1) the data subject has the right to obtain from the controller the erasure of personal data concerning him or her and the controller has the obligation to erase them` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 17(1) erase the personal data without undue delay`
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- "without undue delay" is not a number, so no WITHIN is written and no deadline is invented (NOTES, Rules with no breach path)

§ `Article 17(2): informing other controllers`

-- src:234 | 2. Where the controller has made the personal data public and is obliged pursuant to paragraph 1 to erase the personal data, the controller, taking account of available technology and the cost of implementation, shall take reasonable steps, including technical measures, to inform controllers which are processing the personal data that the data subject has requested the erasure by such controllers of any links to, or copy or replication of, those personal data.
@ref Art 17(2) (src:234)
GIVEN `the controller has made the personal data public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller is obliged pursuant to paragraph 1 to erase the personal data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 17(3) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the controller has taken reasonable steps, including technical measures, taking account of available technology and the cost of implementation, to inform controllers which are processing the personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 17(2) the controller takes reasonable steps, including technical measures, to inform controllers which are processing the personal data that the data subject has requested the erasure of any links to, or copy or replication of, those personal data` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the controller has made the personal data public`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b)): "Where the controller has made the personal data public and is obliged pursuant to paragraph 1 to erase the personal data"
        IF `Art 17(3) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "shall not apply"): "Paragraphs 1 and 2 shall not apply to the extent that processing is necessary"
        IF `the controller is obliged pursuant to paragraph 1 to erase the personal data` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "Where", periods ruling (b)): "and is obliged pursuant to paragraph 1 to erase the personal data"
        IF `the controller is obliged pursuant to paragraph 1 to erase the personal data` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the controller is obliged under paragraph 1 is the answer of `Art 17(1) ...`, and it does not answer on these facts
        IF `the controller has taken reasonable steps, including technical measures, taking account of available technology and the cost of implementation, to inform controllers which are processing the personal data`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        IF `Art 17(3) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): no steps were taken, and whether paragraph 3 takes the duty away is not decided by the facts the caller gave
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "the controller, taking account of available technology and the cost of implementation, shall take reasonable steps, including technical measures, to inform controllers which are processing the personal data"
    -- "reasonable": an undefined term; a plain fact the caller states.

GIVEN `the controller has made the personal data public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller is obliged pursuant to paragraph 1 to erase the personal data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Art 17(3) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 17 action`
`Art 17(2) the controller must take reasonable steps to inform the controllers which are processing the personal data` MEANS
    IF `the controller has made the personal data public` AND `the controller is obliged pursuant to paragraph 1 to erase the personal data` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND NOT (`Art 17(3) paragraphs 1 and 2 do not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 17(2) take reasonable steps, including technical measures, to inform the controllers which are processing the personal data of the erasure request`
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- no time limit and no consequence is stated (NOTES, Rules with no breach path)
